nd log the comparison basis.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Escalate out of cadence explicitly and visibly: stop the line, label the action a hot-fix so the exception is on the record."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A decision could carry material risk or irreversible impact.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment 84-105 'STOP-THE-LINE HOT-FIX' declares the intervention; pattern IF: a decision could carry material risk or irreversible impact.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A defect in an evidence-store sibling may carry material risk to the boot-reachable chain, warranting an interruptive decision."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Coordination costs discourage escalation, while risk-blind escalation wastes time on low-stakes work.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment 107-135 'outside normal queue cadence'; pattern HOWEVER: coordination costs discourage escalation while risk-blind escalation wastes time.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Normal queue cadence would defer the fix (coordination discipline), but waiting risks letting a high-stakes defect ride the queue."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Estimate risk cost (impact x likelihood) and compare it to coordination cost. Escalate when risk cost exceeds a defined threshold, and log the comparison basis.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: preserves speed on low-stakes actions while protecting high-stakes decisions; the fragment names both the stop and the cadence exception.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Marking the exception preserves queue speed for ordinary work while protecting the high-stakes fix from cadence delay."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [1], :pattern "agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk"} {:pattern-rationale "Delegating via a tracked issue is chosen over leaving work idle, acknowledging coordination cost as a real spend.", :fragment-span {:start 139, :end 200}, :occurrence-id ["agent/coordination-has-cost" 2], :roles ["action" "dependency"], :source-sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a", :sentence-id "s1", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/coordination-has-cost", :objects {:G {:text "    Cost-aware coordination prevents both under-use (never asking for help when stuck) and over-use (constant interruption). It respects the resources of collaborators.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'handed to Codex via GitHub issue #65'; pattern THEN: include coordination cost in decision-making unless risk of error is higher than the cost.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Spend the coordination cost deliberately once, on a tracked issue, rather than piecemeal or not at all — the risk of the siblings stalling exceeds the handoff cost."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent wants to leverage external capabilities or get authoritative answers.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Fragment 139-200: work 'handed to Codex'; pattern IF: the agent wants to leverage external capabilities.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Finishing the three siblings needs work the author is not doing itself, so external capability (Codex) is being leveraged."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Coordination is not free: it takes time, consumes attention, introduces latency, and may require context transfer. Treating it as free leads to over-reliance or spamming.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: coordination takes time, attention, and context transfer; the fragment shows the cost being paid via a written GitHub issue.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Delegating costs something: authoring the issue, transferring context, and accepting latency on the siblings' completion."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Model coordination as an action with explicit cost (latency, tokens, human attention units). Include this cost in decision-making: sometimes working with partial local knowledge is better than waiting for external input, unless the risk of error is higher than the coordination cost.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: cost-aware coordination prevents under-use and over-use; the single consolidated issue covering all three siblings is the observed shape.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "One explicit coordination artifact prevents both under-use (siblings left idle) and over-use (repeated interruptions), respecting Codex's attention."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [2], :pattern "agent/coordination-has-cost"}], :edges [{:from ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 0], :to ["agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk" 1], :kind :contrasts-with, :from-fragment 0, :to-fragment 1, :from-roles ["action" "goal"], :to-roles ["contrast" "context"]} {:from ["agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk" 1], :to ["agent/coordination-has-cost" 2], :kind :contex