decisions, open questions, next actions.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Transfer the remaining work through a durable, tracked handoff record — GitHub issue #65 — rather than an untracked mention."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Continuity matters: the work is incremental, context is expensive to rebuild, or progress would be lost.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Fragment 139-200: 'Three remaining siblings handed to Codex via GitHub issue #65'; pattern IF: continuity matters, context is expensive to rebuild.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The three remaining siblings are incremental work whose context (what INSTANTIATE already established) is expensive to rebuild."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Without explicit handoff, successors face cold starts: they repeat discoveries, miss constraints, or contradict prior decisions.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: without explicit handoff, successors face cold starts; the fragment records the transfer to a new agent.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Handing work to a different agent risks a cold start: Codex could repeat discoveries or miss the decisions already made for the completed sibling."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Define a handoff record that captures: current state hypothesis, decisions made and why, open questions, scope boundaries, next actions, evidence/trail anchors, and any provisional-claim ledger. Emit it at session end or when transferring to another agent.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: handoffs convert ephemeral session state into persistent project state; the tracked issue number in the fragment is the persistent anchor.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The issue converts ephemeral session state into persistent project state so the sibling work continues asynchronously without context collapse."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [2], :pattern "agent/handoff-preserves-context"} {:pattern-rationale "Delegating via a tracked issue is chosen over leaving work idle, acknowledging coordination cost as a real spend.", :fragment-span {:start 139, :end 200}, :occurrence-id ["agent/coordination-has-cost" 2], :roles ["action" "dependency"], :source-sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a", :sentence-id "s1", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/coordination-has-cost", :objects {:G {:text "    Cost-aware coordination prevents both under-use (never asking for help when stuck) and over-use (constant interruption). It respects the resources of collaborators.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'handed to Codex via GitHub issue #65'; pattern THEN: include coordination cost in decision-making unless risk of error is higher than the cost.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Spend the coordination cost deliberately once, on a tracked issue, rather than piecemeal or not at all — the risk of the siblings stalling exceeds the handoff cost."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent wants to leverage external capabilities or get authoritative answers.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Fragment 139-200: work 'handed to Codex'; pattern IF: the agent wants to leverage external capabilities.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Finishing the three siblings needs work the author is not doing itself, so external capability (Codex) is being leveraged."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Coordination is not free: it takes time, consumes attention, introduces latency, and may require context transfer. Treating it as free leads to over-reliance or spamming.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: coordination takes time, attention, and context transfer; the fragment shows the cost being paid via a written GitHub issue.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Delegating costs something: authoring the issue, transferring context, and accepting latency on the siblings' completion."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Model coordination as an action with explicit cost (latency, tokens, human attention units). Include this cost in decision-making: sometimes working with partial local knowledge is better than waiting for external input, unless the risk of error is higher than the coordination cost.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: cost-aware coordination prevents under-use and over-use; the single consolidated issue covering all three siblings is the observed shape.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "One explicit coordination artifact prevents both under-use (siblings left idle) and over-use (repeated interruptions), respecting Codex's attention."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [2], :pattern "agent/coordination-has-cost"}], :edges [{:from ["agent/handoff-preserves-context" 2], :to ["agent/coordination-has-cost" 2], :kind :